<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mutare</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Umtali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mutare, called Umtali until 1982, is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. Founded in the 1890s and moved to its present site to meet the railway from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beira">Beira</a>, which reached it in 1898, it became the gateway between the Rhodesian interior and the coast. It is the capital of Manicaland Province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mutare.jpg" alt="Mutare" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seabifar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutare_aerial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
